@startuml
title Registration & Verification Flow (Core with providers)

actor Person

participant "VerificationController" as VC
participant "GuestUser" as GU
participant "UserService" as US
participant "RegisteredUser" as RU
participant "VerificationService" as VS
participant "PhoneVerificationProvider" as PP
participant "TwilioSmsSender" as TW
participant "VerificationSendLog" as SL
participant "EmailVerificationProvider" as EP
participant "SmtpSender" as SM
participant "SmartIdVerificationProvider" as SP
participant "VerificationPolicy" as VP
participant "VerificationRules" as VR
participant "ShelterService" as SS
database "Database" as DB

== 0. Anonymous browsing ==
note over Person, GU
  The map is public (VIEW_MAP is the baseline capability in
  VerificationRules.ofDefaults()) - no canWatch() method exists:
  guests simply can't write. (canWatch was removed in the review-fix pass.)
end note

== 1. Register ==
Person -> US : register(name, email, phone)
US -> RU : new RegisteredUser(...)
note over Person, US
  The profile carries no password: it is stored by the AUTH
  context (03-auth.puml): AuthService.register ->
  PasswordHasher.hash -> UserCredentialsRepository.save.
  Profile vs credentials are separate aggregates.
end note
US -> DB : save(RegisteredUser)
US --> Person : RegisteredUser (levels = {})

== 1b. Verification over HTTP (JWT required) ==
note over Person, VC
  Step 2 gap closed: verification is now reachable via
  POST /verify/request + POST /verify/confirm (Bearer JWT
  required; user resolved from the token, never the body).
  SMART_ID -> 400 up front (stub in v1).
end note
note over VC, VS
  Anti-spam (Twilio plan): per-IP token bucket in the controller
  (ClientIps) + resend cooldown + per-user daily cap in the
  service (VerificationSendLog, file-backed, survives restarts).
  Violations -> 429 with the uniform ErrorResponse.
end note

== 2. Phone verification: request OTP ==
Person -> VC : POST /verify/request {level=PHONE}
VC -> VS : requestVerification(user, PHONE)
VS -> SL : lastSentAt / countToday(userId, PHONE)  (cooldown + daily cap)
alt within limits
VS -> PP : request(user)
PP -> TW : sendSms(phone, "OpenShelter OTP: 123456")   ' AppInfo.APP_DISPLAY_NAME + " OTP: " + otp
TW --> PP : sent
PP --> VS : PendingVerification(PHONE, codeHash, expiry)
VS -> DB : save pending
VS -> SL : record(userId, PHONE, phone, now)
VC --> Person : 202
else throttled
VC --> Person : 429
end

== 3. Phone verification: confirm OTP ==
Person -> VC : POST /verify/confirm {level=PHONE, code}
VC -> VS : confirmVerification(user, PHONE, otp)
VS -> PP : confirm(user, pending, otp)
PP --> VS : true (hash + attempts + expiry check)
VS -> DB : save VerificationClaim(PHONE, provider=sms)
VS --> VC : true
VC -> DB : save(user) - persists the new claim
VC --> Person : 200 | 400

== 4. Email verification: request token ==
Person -> VC : POST /verify/request {level=EMAIL}
VC -> VS : requestVerification(user, EMAIL)
VS -> EP : request(user)
EP -> SM : send(email, "OpenShelter verification code: abcdef12")   ' AppInfo.APP_DISPLAY_NAME + " verification code: " + 8-char token
SM --> EP : sent
EP --> VS : PendingVerification(EMAIL, tokenHash, expiry)
VS -> DB : save pending
VC --> Person : 202

== 5. Email verification: confirm token ==
Person -> VC : POST /verify/confirm {level=EMAIL, code}
VC -> VS : confirmVerification(user, EMAIL, token)
VS -> EP : confirm(user, pending, token)
EP --> VS : true
VS -> DB : save VerificationClaim(EMAIL, provider=smtp)
VS --> VC : true
VC -> DB : save(user) - persists the new claim
VC --> Person : 200 | 400

== 6. Smart-ID: stub ==
note over Person, SP
  Smart-ID: STUB in v1. Future flow = start session + poll;
  the provider proves identity itself via PKI - no stored code.
  The controller rejects SMART_ID requests with 400 up front.
end note

== 7. Capability check ==
Person -> RU : canWrite()
RU -> VP : allows({PHONE, EMAIL}, SUBMIT_SHELTER)
VP -> VR : rules (baseline + byLevel)
VR --> VP : {PHONE, EMAIL} -> {VIEW_MAP, SUBMIT_SHELTER}
VP --> RU : true
RU --> Person : true

== 8. Add a shelter (write) ==
Person -> SS : addPlace(user, shelter)
SS -> RU : canWrite()
RU --> SS : true
SS -> DB : save shelter (status = ACTIVE)
SS --> Person : submitted (published immediately - community reports + confirmation govern quality)

' Email = same two-phase shape (request -> confirm).
' Smart-ID = future session + polling (stub in v1).
' No moderator: quality governed by community reports + confirmation
' (ReviewStatus on the shelter - see 05-shelter-api.puml).
@enduml